  "body": "## What changed\n- **AGENTS.md, \"A claim comment is a claim\"**: a contributor's claim no longer stands just because its comment exists.\n  - It is **live** while one of these holds: an open PR for the issue; a commit on the claimant's branch in the last 48 hours; a comment by the claimant on the issue in the last 48 hours. Research claims have no branch, so the comment keeps them live.\n  - Otherwise it is **stale**: it is not mirrored into a `claimed` label, and a label already behind it is removed with a comment that says why and how to claim again.\n  - A claim also **ends** when its comment is deleted, when the claimant's last comment withdraws it (`unclaim`, \"releasing this claim\", \"claim withdrawn\", \"the issue is free\"), or when the maintainer releases it. An ended claim is never mirrored back from its old comment; only a new `claimed:` comment is a claim again.\n  - \"Claim before any code\", \"Check before claiming\", \"Mirror it\" and \"Maintenance\" are reworded to match. The 4 h rule for the owner account's own agents is unchanged.\n- **`.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md`, step 4**: the mirror pass skips stale and ended claims (with the commands to check liveness); the withdraw pass releases stale claims and recognises the release wordings.\n- **`.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`** 13 -> 14.\n\n## Why\nMaintainer, 2026-11-11: \"unclaim those 8 old ones and let someone pick em up and fix em they can't stall\" and \"Yes implement stale claim rule\". Eight issues (#26, #287, #363, #485, #586, #621, #637, #688) were locked by claim comments days old with no work in progress behind them; a maintenance sweep following the old rule had just re-labelled them `claimed`.\n\n## How tested\n- No code changed; no gate applies.\n- The rule was applied by hand on the eight issues above today, and the maintenance session has been running the same liveness test since.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The `gh api .../commits?sha=<branch>` liveness command in the skill was not run against a fork branch in this PR.\n\n## For forks\nPull the process files at PROCESS_VERSION 14. What changes for a contributor: a claim comment holds an issue for 48 hours on its own; after that it needs an open PR, a recent commit on the branch, or a comment on the issue to stay live. A released claim is renewed with a new `claimed:` comment.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
